  "title": "Chapter 10 – Community Health Nursing",
  "order": 10,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "nd747mv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Community Health Nursing applies public health concepts to preserve, promote, and restore health across populations.",
        "Levels of Disease Prevention encompass primary (health promotion/protection), secondary (early diagnosis/treatment), and tertiary (rehabilitation).",
        "Primary Health Care is essential health care made universally accessible to individuals and families in the community.",
        "Maternal and Child Health Services (MCH) and basic immunization schedules form the cornerstone of preventive health nursing.",
        "National Health Programs in India target major communicable and non-communicable diseases through structured public health interventions."
      ],
      "id": "7csoi8x"
    },
